  "description": "Ninety-seven Visium sections from twelve glioblastoma patients, several regions per tumour, and the snRNA-seq atlas of about one million nuclei they are mapped with, as published by the Bayraktar group on WebAtlas. Patient AT15's nine sections are Visium CytAssist 11 mm (about 11,000 spots and an 18,202-gene probe panel), so their counts run about ten times higher than the other sections'. Raw data: ArrayExpress E-MTAB-17164 (Visium) and E-MTAB-17183 (Multiome).",
